 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Climate change is a long-term change in the Earth's weather patterns, mainly global warming (a rise in average temperature).\nCause: the greenhouse effect is increased. Greenhouse gases (carbon dioxide, methane, nitrous oxide, water vapour) trap heat in the atmosphere. Humans add more by:\n• burning fossil fuels (petrol, diesel, coal, gas) in cars, factories and generators;\n• cutting and burning forests (deforestation, bush fires) — trees take in carbon dioxide;\n• rotting rubbish and rice fields and cattle (methane).\nEffects: hotter weather, droughts (the Sahel, Lake Chad shrinking), floods, rising sea levels, crop failure and hunger, spread of diseases like malaria, loss of plants and animals.\nPrevention: plant trees, stop bush fires, save energy, use solar and hydroelectric power, walk or cycle, reduce and recycle waste.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "x": "cutting down forests"
  },
  "problem": "Explain how {x} adds to global warming.",
  "steps": [
   "Trees take in carbon dioxide for photosynthesis; fewer trees take in less.",
   "Burning the cut trees also releases carbon dioxide."
  ],
  "answer": "More carbon dioxide stays in the air and traps more heat.",
  "checks": []
 },
